{
  "_about": "Defaults of the vocal performance engine (scripts/vocal_engine). Every section can be overridden by a vocal preset or a track's vocal config. Values are literature-informed starting points (Rosenberg/LF glottal pulse, Klatt resonators, nasal-murmur formants), NOT tuned by ear and NOT from the knowledgebase. Audition before trusting them. `technique` holds what the singer does with the tract (ring, formant tuning, vowel cover, creak); `consonants` is the syllable inventory, each entry a physical recipe.",
  "sources": [
    "Rosenberg 1971, 'Effect of glottal pulse shape on the quality of natural vowels', JASA 49",
    "Fant, Liljencrants, Lin 1985, 'A four-parameter model of glottal flow', STL-QPSR 4",
    "Klatt 1980, 'Software for a cascade/parallel formant synthesizer', JASA 67",
    "Fujimura 1962 / Dang, Honda, Suzuki 1994 on nasal murmur formants and the /m/ anti-resonance",
    "Sundberg 1987, 'The Science of the Singing Voice' (singer's formant, vibrato 5-7 Hz)",
    "Sundberg 1975, 'Formant technique in a professional female singer', Acustica 32 (formant tuning above F1)",
    "Klatt 1980 (F4/F5 targets, five-pole cascade reference)",
    "Peterson & Barney 1952, 'Control methods used in a study of the vowels', JASA 24 (F1-F3 of /ae/, /E/, /I/, /O/)",
    "Ohman 1966, 'Coarticulation in VCV utterances', JASA 39 (anticipatory vowel-to-vowel coarticulation)",
    "Titze 1994, 'Principles of Voice Production' (period jitter ~0.5-1 %, shimmer ~3-5 %)",
    "Ladefoged & Johnson, 'A Course in Phonetics' (voice-onset time 30-90 ms, fricative spectra)"
  ],
